    description: "**Symptom.** Invoking `hypergumbo routes --input bm.json` (a read-only command consuming a pre-built behavior map) writes 5 sketch artifact files to disk as a side effect of the invocation. This was observed during the pass-14 correction of dogfooding finding YYY (originally INV-pomol-horid-...).\n\n**Expected.** A read-only inspection subcommand should not write artifacts to disk. Side effects belong on `run` and explicit `sketch` / `compact` subcommands.\n\n**Scope.** Confirmed on `hypergumbo routes --input <bm.json>`. Other read-only subcommands that accept `--input` (search, slice, explain, symbols, io-boundaries, verify-claims, test-coverage, dead-code-maybe, routes, compact) have not been audited for the same pattern. The 5 specific artifacts written by routes were not enumerated in the original YYY observation; reproduction needed.\n\n**Exposure.** Side-effect filesystem writes during nominally-read-only CLI invocation.\n\n**Consequence.** Read-only invocations leave artifacts behind, confusing users about what each command does. May overwrite or conflict with intentional sketch outputs from prior commands. Reproducibility of read-only commands is undermined.\n\n**Origin.** Discovered as a residual sub-finding while correcting YYY (s13 dogfooding) in s14 of the dogfooding cycle. YYY's primary substance (a positional-swallow bug) was traced to OOOO (INV-jibof). YYY-(a) residual (schema organization — no top-level `routes` field in bm.json) is a docs/spec issue, not filed separately. YYY-(b) — this item — is the routes-side-effect residual filed in the substrate reorganization (post-s20).\n\n**Audit needed.** Enumerate which other read-only subcommands write sketch artifacts; either confirm routes is unique or expand scope."  # 24f7
    fields:  # 24f7
      severity: "low"  # 24f7
      statement: "Read-only inspection subcommands invoked with --input MUST NOT write artifact files to disk. Side effects are reserved for run, sketch, and compact."  # 24f7
      root_cause: "routes subcommand triggers sketch artifact emission as a side effect of its read path; the read path does not isolate from the artifact-writing code shared with run/sketch."  # 24f7
